{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kunobi-ninja/kache/pulls/1491","id":4809787220,"node_id":"PR_kwDORRBv5c8AAAABHq-HVA","html_url":"https://github.com/kunobi-ninja/kache/pull/1491","diff_url":"https://github.com/kunobi-ninja/kache/pull/1491.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/kunobi-ninja/kache/pull/1491.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kunobi-ninja/kache/issues/1491","number":1491,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"fix: false hits, incremental edit loops and full-disk recovery before 1.1","user":{"login":"jleni","id":13698520,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNjk4NTIw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13698520?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jleni","html_url":"https://github.com/jleni","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jleni/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jleni/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jleni/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jleni/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jleni/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jleni/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jleni/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jleni/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jleni/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"More fixes to land before tagging 1.1. Each commit stands alone, and its message has the detail.\n\nTwo more commits are in review and will be pushed to this branch: Cargo's home inside the project will no longer change the key of a package whose build script declares nothing, and a crate starting its incremental state will no longer make builds in other checkouts wait for it.\n\n## What changes for users\n\n### Stale artifacts\n\n- A file saved in the same clock tick as Kache read it no longer pins an old hash. Kache remembers a hash only if the file's timestamps had settled, counts a write just before the build as a write, and checks a file again after reading it under the guard.\n- C/C++: the preprocessor memo trusts only settled timestamps, and a key-first store is refused when a keyed input was written during the build or just before it. Entries stored before these fixes are re-keyed. An input that a generator rewrites right before every compile is never cached.\n- With `KACHE_MODIFIED_INPUT_GUARD` on, a keyed input that is gone, or whose size, write time or inode changed after the key was taken, now refuses the store, as the docs already said.\n- Input predictions check every workspace or path crate against a digest of its tree, not only crates with a proc-macro dependency. A file added to a directory that a re-exported macro lists (`sqlx::migrate!`, `include_dir!`) is now compiled in. Kache's cache and runtime directories and Cargo's home are left out of that digest when a CI job keeps them inside the project, as GitLab requires.\n- The files and environment variables a build script declares with `cargo:rerun-if-changed` and `cargo:rerun-if-env-changed` now key every rustc unit of its workspace or path package. A script that declares nothing keys the package's non-Rust files. A result whose declared inputs moved during the compile is not stored.\n- A build-script run recorded without the outside files it read is no longer restored, and seeding a new target recognises forward-slash and other Windows spellings of the donor path.\n\n### Incremental edit loops\n\n- A compile error keeps the crate's incremental state, as plain Cargo does. Before, the fix and the next edit both compiled the crate in full. An ICE, a signal, or rustc reporting broken incremental files still resets it.\n- A workspace library you edit while building another package (`cargo build -p app`, a workspace with a root package, a build from a member directory) gets the same incremental treatment as the crate you build, after one full compile.\n- These incremental compiles are not stored, so a pull or branch switch counts as editing. A CI job that keeps `target/` between runs with Cargo's incremental on should set `KACHE_ADAPTIVE_INCREMENTAL=0` or `CARGO_INCREMENTAL=0`.\n- `KACHE_INCREMENTAL_CRATES` now covers a listed crate whether or not the command selects it.\n- The docs now say when an adapted unit checks the cache again: after eight builds, or 15 minutes without one.\n\n### Disk and cleanup\n\n- Free-space recovery works on a full volume, and a store refused for lack of space asks for recovery.\n- A build that waits for target cleanup says so instead of looking hung. Cleanup no longer holds builds back while it deletes a renamed target, and a target rebuilt during its own deletion stays tracked.\n\n### Remote\n\n- A selected AWS profile that cannot supply credentials now fails with an error naming the profile, instead of falling through to web identity, ECS or the EC2 instance role. A non-empty `AWS_PROFILE` counts as a selection: on EC2, unset it if it only sets a region. Empty `AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID` and `AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY` count as unset, and one without the other is an error.\n\n## Upgrade notes\n\n- The first open of an index adds the new memo columns and rebuilds the file-hash memo and the C/C++ memo once. Switching between 1.0.x and this build afterwards does not repeat it; this was checked in both orders against the installed 1.0.0. A 1.0.x GC that rebuilds the file-hash table drops the new column, and the next open restores it.\n- Each C/C++ unit compiles once after the upgrade, and so does each rustc unit of a workspace or path package with a build script.\n- After a workspace change, each workspace crate runs dependency discovery once on its next build. A workspace past 20,000 entries discovers on every build.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- macOS (rustc 1.99.0): fmt, clippy `-D warnings`, about 2,960 unit tests, 563 store tests, and all 35 integration test binaries (367 tests).\n- Linux (x86_64, 1.98.0) and Windows (`x86_64-pc-windows-msvc`) clippy `-D warnings` through cross builds. Their tests run here for the first time, and `adaptive_incremental_workspace_test` is the first real seed-and-active cycle on Windows CI.\n- Edit loop on a synthetic workspace, macOS, private caches, debug binaries, medians:\n\n| Step | Plain Cargo | main | This branch |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Fix after a type error | 1.10 s | 10.06 s | 1.09 s |\n| Next edit | 1.11 s | 8.77 s | 1.07 s |\n| `cargo build -p app`, edits 2-5 | 1.22-1.53 s | 7.9-11.1 s | 1.25-1.46 s |\n\n- Cold build of a 30-member workspace with optimized binaries: 2.36 s on this branch against 2.34 s on main (plain Cargo 1.09 s), within noise. Warm rebuild into a new target: 0.39 s against 0.40 s.\n- The first edit of a library the command does not select is about 18% slower than a normal compile, because it starts incremental state from empty.\n- The perf gate cannot see the incremental changes, because its scenarios set `CARGO_INCREMENTAL=0`. Its key_ms and dep_info_runs should show the cost of the tree and declared-input checks.\n","created_at":"2026-10-10T08:07:26Z","updated_at":"2026-10-10T13:46:06Z","closed_at":"2026-10-10T13:46:03Z","merged_at":"2026-10-10T13:46:03Z","merge_commit_sha":"d74b0d58351683c570177a3349e7447e2feda4e2","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[{"login":"emmanuelm41","id":10941036,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwOTQxMDM2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10941036?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/emmanuelm41","html_url":"https://github.com/emmanuelm41","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emmanuelm41/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emmanuelm41/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emmanuelm41/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emmanuelm41/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emmanuelm41/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https: